  "created": "2026-08-28T08:50:27.063Z",
  "description": "Abstract duplex byte-stream provider consumed by Iec61850.Transport: supplies either a plaintext TCP stream or a TLS 1.2/1.3 stream per IEC 62351-3, so every layer above Transport (Session, Presentation, ACSE, MMS, ACSI, Server, Client) remains completely unaware of whether TLS is in use. Also owns certificate/trust-store lifecycle and credential-redaction helpers for PDU logging. Deliberately has no dependencies of its own -- it sits alongside Asn1Ber as a foundation module, not downstream of Transport or Acse.",
  "id": "Iec61850.Security",
